      "problem": "An arithmetic sequence has ${a}_{3}=18$ and ${a}_{4}=23.$ What is the common difference of the sequence?",
      "worked_solution": "The first thing to note is that the terms are *increasing*, and therefore we expect the common difference $d$ to be *positive*.\n\nSince the two terms are consecutive, we can find the common difference by subtracting ${a}_{3}$ from ${a}_{4}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{4}-{a}_{3} \\\\  & =23-18 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the common difference is $d=5.$",
